Subject: up: DMA snapshot miss waits for its flush entry only (EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_WAIT)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (no upstream port). Gated by EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_WAIT (exact 1), a
live switch (Id DmaMissWait, not armed); off by default. Only a plain DMA snapshot miss in
Maxwell3D::FrontDmaRead (split front, EDEN_NX2_DMA_SNAPSHOT) takes it: the front waits until the
back ran everything sent (new GpuSplit::WaitForSent), not also for the back's idle hook and
back_quiet. Ignored (full drain, one warning) with EDEN_NX2_READBACK_WAIT on.
EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_WAIT_VERIFY=1 (boot) drains in full anyway and compares the words. 10 s line
while on: "EDEN_UP_DMA_MISS_WAIT: N misses waited ...".

Reviewed draft from the draws job, v2: reviewer moved the switch read from every FrontDmaRead
(about 20k/s, 92% hits) into the plain-miss branch only, so hits, the snapshot verify and the
L1028 narrowed path never read it; re-wrapped one comment. Gain and test metric corrected in
the review (L949 idle hooks and sleeps, not "a drain's hook").
